# The TextMate grammar is generated by the language server repo's build-grammar
# script, which writes LF. Pin it so core.autocrlf cannot leave the file showing
# as modified after every regeneration when nothing actually changed.
syntaxes/*.json text eol=lf

# Shell scripts, whose line endings are otherwise decided by the checkout: with
# core.autocrlf on Windows, `scripts/e2e.sh` comes out of a clone with CRLF, and
# whether that matters then depends on the shell. Git Bash strips the CR, so the
# script runs; WSL and a plain POSIX sh do not, and each line's last token keeps
# a trailing CR — which for this script means `unset ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE` unsets
# a differently-named variable and the run dies with MODULE_NOT_FOUND, the exact
# failure the script exists to prevent. Pinning removes the guesswork, and stops
# the file showing as modified whenever a tool rewrites it with LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
